    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0428" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg394"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Romero to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexican Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have had the honor to receive
                    your note, No. 255, dated yesterday, with which you were pleased to accompany
                    copy of the information which the Acting Commissioner of Indian Affairs directed
                    to the Secretary of the Interior the 12th instant, respecting the incident of
                    the Yuma Indians who have illegally occupied the lands of the ranch Algodones,
                    and whose removal the Mexican Government asked.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you in reply that I already transmitted to my
                    Government your note and the information attached thereto, in order that in view
                    of the considerations expressed in both documents it may determine what may seem
                    convenient.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Romero.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
